In my current game, I noticed a peculiar difference between pet dragons
grown up from a baby dragon and tamed full-fledged dragons.  I doubt
that it is intended.

I am playing a chaotic ice mage. He acquired the charm monster spell
early and a magic whistle as well, so he took the habit of charming baby
dragons, which otherwise would still bite him a lot. Unfortunately, he
prayed too early when getting weak and his god was displeased, but he
survived that event, snacking on a gnome shortly after. Since there was
an attended altar at Dlvl 10, I decided to try and have taken out the
minetown priest by my pets. This worked to my surprise, two baby dragons
can kill a priest. I then sacrificed and converted the altar, which
however angered the lawful god Air. He sent in a monadic and a movanic
deva. I was in no shape to battle them, so read my emergency blessed
scroll of teleportation and escaped to the staircase. Whistled in my
pets, went upstairs. After some thinking, I decided on the following
approach: move on downwards to the bottom of the mines and have the
dragon babies kill as many gnomes and gnome warriors on Ruggo's level as
possible. One might become a dragon that could take out the devas (later
I learned that my god had already been appeased by the altar conversion,
so my fears I could not pray anymore were unnecessary).

The plan worked in part. One of the baby dragons grew to adult form, but
after going upstairs we encountered a flesh golem that he was not able
to hit. I was surprised, because I remembered that as a doppelganger in
an earlier game, I did not have any problems killing a statue gargoyle
in dragon form, so I thought dragons automatically hit as a +1 weapon at
least. So there was no question letting him attack the devas because he
would not be able to hit them.

I skipped minetown and continued the game. Much later, in the Wyrm
Caves, I was able to charm two adult dragons. Shimmy, my previous baby
pet dragon, also grown up, was still with me (and still is, he is a
survivor, the others have already died). The funny thing is, he still
cannot hit a statue gargoyle but the other dragons could without any
problem.

So it seems that an adult dragon does indeed hit like a +1 weapon at
least, but only if it was adult to begin with. A baby dragon pet that
becomes adult, still does not hit like an enchanted weapon.  This looks
like a bug to me, or is there any rationale behind it?

